{
  "dom_id": "step-q4553",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2032}(2)$ if $f(x)={\\int }_{2}^{2x}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}-t}\\,\\text{d}t.$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute ${f}^{\u2032}(x),$ we first make the substitution $u=2x$ and then we apply the chain rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{2}^{2x}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}{\\int }_{2}^{u}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integrand is continuous on $[2,u],$ and so by FTC II we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\cdot \\sqrt{{u}^{3}-u} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)\\cdot \\sqrt{(2x)^{3}-(2x)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{8{x}^{3}-2x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${f}^{\u2032}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(2) & =2\\sqrt{8(2)^{3}-2(2)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{64-4} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{15}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
